    Do not install the full CXF feature (#8222)
    
    The ext-core feature pulled in the complete `cxf` Karaf feature,
    although Opencast only uses CXF's JAX-RS implementation, which is
    already installed through `cxf-jaxrs`, `cxf-http-jetty` and
    `cxf-rs-description-openapi-v3`. The full feature additionally installs
    the SOAP/JAX-WS stack, CORBA (JacORB), JMS, UDP, WS-Addressing, WS-RM,
    WS-Policy, WS-Security (WSS4J, OpenSAML, xmlsec), Aegis, the JavaScript
    frontend (Rhino), Ehcache, metrics and more, none of which is used by
    any Opencast bundle.
    
    Two bundles from that set are mandatory imports of other bundles we
    install, which is why they are now listed explicitly:
    
    - bcel, imported by Xalan
    - mina-core, imported by spring-security-ldap
    
    Effect on a develop distribution (all-in-one, H2, idle after startup),
    mean of 12 boots per variant (6 cold, 6 warm), ± standard deviation:
    
    ```
                                      full cxf        without      change
      installed bundles                    423            379     -44 (-10%)
      time to first HTTP 200       8.5 s ± 0.5    7.7 s ± 0.4    -0.8 s (-9%)
      time to all REST endpoints   8.8 s ± 0.5    8.3 s ± 0.4    -0.5 s (-6%)
      CPU time during startup           40.3 s         40.7 s    none
      heap used after full GC         176.5 MB       169.1 MB    -7.4 MB (-4%)
      metaspace                       128.6 MB       127.6 MB    -1.0 MB
      loaded classes                    21,032         20,823    -210 (-1%)
      RSS                        1037 MB ± 70   1020 MB ± 56    within noise
      system/ directory                 464 MB         439 MB    -25 MB
    ```
    
    The removed bundles were installed but hardly ever loaded, hence the
    small effect on memory. The main gain is a smaller runtime with fewer
    third-party libraries to keep track of.
    
